{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 11, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1410", :event/action "Added India (:IND) as a 4th jurisdiction to apparel.facts/catalog (was VNM/BGD/USA), one of the remaining 3 pre-screened candidates from iteration 6's classification pass (isic-1430/1512 remain queued). Citations: Factories Act 1948 Section 6 (plant registration/licensing, HIGH confidence -- read directly on indiacode.nic.in) + Sections 51/54 (48hr/week, 9hr/day working-hours limits, MODERATE-HIGH confidence -- corroborated across multiple independent secondary legal sources rather than fetched from primary text directly, disclosed as such rather than overstated) + IS 15798:2007 (Bureau of Indian Standards textile-labeling requirements, HIGH confidence -- downloaded and read directly). Also found, and deliberately did NOT cite, that the Ministry of Textiles/BIS are actively drafting new stricter labeling rules this same week (per contemporaneous news coverage) -- not yet in force, so only the existing current standard was cited rather than the still-draft one.", :event/verification "clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 28 tests / 110 assertions, 0 failures both times (this repo's existing tests already used >= count checks, no pre-existing assertion needed fixing). Independently re-spot-checked the IS 15798:2007 PDF and the indiacode.nic.in Section 6 page myself before writing the citations (confirmed exact title/content match) rather than trusting a single search-result summary. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1410-ind-apparel-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1410/merges, commit 1cda0abce6c9fc627bde617a2ec0eea6f17a8e7d) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 79e2af671bdc -> 1cda0abce6c9 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positi