{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 22, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bih", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Bosnia and Herzegovina (BIH) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/14/16/18/20. This is the most constitutionally complex jurisdiction this loop has scaffolded: a STATE level, TWO Entities (Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina/FBiH, Republika Srpska/RS), plus Brčko District, with overlapping/exclusive competencies. Delegated to a fresh background agent with an explicit instruction to investigate rather than assume which level each competency actually operates at. Delivered: marketentry.facts (found public procurement IS genuinely state-level and unified -- the Zakon o javnim nabavkama establishes both the Agencija za javne nabavke and a complaints-review body URŽ as state institutions sharing ONE joint e-procurement portal by the law's own explicit naming, Čl. 14(5) -- a 2-body-but-1-portal shape not previously seen; found company/business REGISTRATION, by contrast, has NO state-level registrar at all -- FBiH and RS each run their own court-based registry system under their own statute, and FBiH/RS further differ in application front-end (RS's APIF one-stop-shop service vs FBiH's direct-to-court filing) -- correcting an initial secondary-source assumption that APIF replaced the RS court, verified false by reading the primary law's own Art. 2 definitions; found a genuinely new split-by-institutional-level shape for the tax-ID system -- an Entity-level 13-digit PIB/JIB assigned first on registration, from which a SEPARATE state-level 12-digit UIO indirect-tax number is then mathematically DERIVED (not independently issued) by programmatically stripping a shared leading digit; found the procurement law's own Čl. 46(2) explicitly cross-recognizes registration documents 'regardless of which level of government issued them' -- a direct textual acknowledgment of the multi-level reality from inside the state law itself; found the tax/social-security-arrears exclusion ground (Čl. 45) is a BINARY exclusion with no de-minimis carve-out, the opposite shape from a prior sibling's percentage-of-turnover threshold) + statute.facts (added a NEW :statute/level field -- :state/:fbih/:rs -- to the shared schema, since no prior sibling needed one; state-level Law on Personal Data Protection (a brand-new 2025 law establishing the same AZLP continuously from its 2006 predecessor); separate FBiH and RS labour laws, since labour law is Entity-level with no state-level labour code at all; separate FBiH and RS business-registration acts). Brčko District's own statutes were honestly NOT investigated within budget -- an explicit, disclosed gap, not silently extrapolated from FBiH+RS coverage.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session (not merely re-reading the agent's report): (1) fresh standalone clone confirmed the diff touches exactly the 16 intended files and src/culture + test/culture are byte-identical to main (empty diff); (2) independently re-fetched and pdftotext-verified all six primary-source citations myself -- the state-level Personal Data Protection Act (WebFetch-confirmed gazette 12/25 + AZLP establishment), FBiH's Zakon o radu (masthead '26/16 i 89/18' matched verbatim), RS's Zakon o radu (repeal clause + adoption number '02/1-021-1715/15' + date '29. decembar 2015' all matched verbatim, corroborating the agent's own MODERATE-not-HIGH confidence calibration on the exact gazette number), FBiH's business-registration act (masthead + 'nadležni registarski sud' language matched), RS's business-registration act (masthead '67 od 8. avgusta 2013' matched, AND independently confirmed the genuinely novel APIF-is-a-service-not-a-registrar finding by reading Čl. 2(g)'s own definition directly -- 'jednošalterski sistem... koje obavlja Agencija' confirms APIF provides the one-stop-shop SERVICE while the court remains the actual registrar), the state procurement law (Čl. 14(5) joint-portal clause, Čl. 17(5) 'e-Nabavke' name, Čl. 92 Agency legal-personality clause, Čl. 93 URŽ's Sarajevo/Banja-Luka/Mostar structure, Čl. 46(2)'s cross-level-recognition clause, and Čl. 45's reprogrammed-payment exception all matched verbatim), and the UIO regulation on the derived tax-ID (Čl. 19-21's exact digit-stripping mechanism -- 'programski oduzme zajednička početna cifra «4»' -- matched verbatim); (3) independently reconstructed the `:local/root` relative-path layout and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 37 tests / 130 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (4) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (5) confirmed origin/main was untouched by the agent before merging. Also noted: the agent's own report flagged that it encountered and correctly disregarded an embedded prompt-injection attempt in a fetched tool result (an instruction to hide a date change) during its research -- handled correctly per the prompt-injection-boundary safety floor, no action needed from this session. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bih/merges, commit 08494eaab7b552b2baed5b64d7dbfead76f1ee64) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced f5dafb81608c -> 08494eaab7b5 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration. Brčko District's own statutes (registration, labor) remain an explicit, disclosed gap for BIH -- a future iteration could extend this catalog if it becomes relevant. Axis alternation is now 11 prod-ready / 11 real-world-ingest-gap across 22 iterations, even