{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 37, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Democratic Republic of the Congo (COD) from a src/culture-only stub, second landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV) dispatched per owner instruction to use subagents for efficient parallel deepening. Delivered: marketentry.facts (Loi n°10/010 du 27 avril 2010 relative aux marches publics, grounding ARMP (Art. 14, a posteriori regulation) and DGCMP (Art. 13, a priori control) as the two-authority procurement-oversight split; live e-procurement portal at armp-rdc.cd/marche.armp-rdc.cd plus a real debarment/blacklist page at armp-rdc.cd/liste-noire/; DRC's OHADA membership (ratified 27 June 2012, in force 12 September 2012) confirmed independently rather than assumed from Benin's precedent; company registration via GUCE (Guichet Unique de Creation d'Entreprise, decree n12/045 + arrete n035/CAB/MIN/J&DH/2013); DGI (tax) created by Decret n17/2003 amended by Decret n22/52) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: a RANKED-CLASSIFICATION recompute against Art. 37's exact 6-tier nationality/ownership preference order (1. Congolese natural person, 2. Congolese-majority-owned SME, 3. Congolese legal person, 4. groupings with Congolese partners/subcontracting, 5. foreign person/entity active in DRC, 6. foreign person/entity from a treaty-partner state) -- distinct from every prior sibling (Bulgaria %-formula, Albania flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia boolean membership, Antigua and Barbuda 3-tier VALUE class, Benin bid-margin recompute, Belize struck-off boolean, Barbados expiry-date recompute, Brunei precedence-ordering, Bhutan sector set-membership, Botswana ordered-tier classification against a 4-item scale) since this is a 6-tier ranked classification against a distinct DRC-specific enumerated order (a similar STRUCTURAL shape to Botswana's ordered-tier check landed earlier in this same batch, but grounded in genuinely different, independently-verified DRC-specific content, not copied). Correctly did NOT model DRC's own Art. 61 discretionary foreign-subcontracting variant (30% subcontract-to-Congolese-firm or 40% Congolese-expert threshold, capped at but not fixed to 5% abattement) -- honestly narrower, mirroring Benin's own prior scope-narrowing discipline on its structurally similar discretionary-margin provision. Statute.facts: OHADA AUSCGIE (independently re-verified: adopted 30 Jan 2014, in force 5 May 2014, NOT copied from Benin's citation text), Code du Travail (Loi n15-2002 amended by Loi n16/010 du 15 juillet 2016). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing: the specific law/decree creating the NIF tax-ID obligation itself (JS-SPA-blocked); DGCMP's own creation-decree number; INSS's founding law; Art. 37/61's discretionary abattement percentages; any populated blacklist entries (mechanism confirmed real, no specific entity claimed). Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md, and independently caught that a stale 'anapi.org' reference in earlier research was actually a hijacked/spam domain -- the real, live ANAPI is anapi.cd (a genuine due-diligence catch, not something merely assumed).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Loi n10/010 PDF myself (armp-rdc.cd, 185KB, 31pp) and read Art. 13 (a priori control), Art. 14 (a posteriori regulation body), Art. 37 (flagship), and Art. 61 (foreign-subcontracting discretionary margin) directly -- Art. 37's exact 6-item list matched verbatim, and Art. 61's exact cap language ('abattement qui ne pourra etre superieure a cinq pourcent') confirmed precisely why the agent correctly declined to model it as a fixed value; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 37 tests / 131 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 37/131/0; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (4) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (5) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 19 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (6) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch feature/market-entry-actor-cod -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod/merges, commit 37471ee6c63e69cf5357d0534616190cbcfc907c) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 8155ff8cf33f -> 37471ee6c63e (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). Applied the commit-and-push-as-SEPARATE-Bash-calls workaround discovered in iteration 36 (the git-push-main-sync-guard hook's regex matches 'git push' anywhere in a compound command string and blocks the ENTIRE chained command atomically before any of it runs, including an earlier git commit in the same invocation).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- second landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA done, COD done, CAF/COG/COM/CPV still in flight). Axis alternation is now 19 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 37 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 37, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:10:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 38, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-com", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Union of the Comoros (COM) from a src/culture-only stub, third landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV). Notably, the delegated agent independently DISCOVERED AND CORRECTED an assumption baked into its own task brief: the brief assumed Comoros was NOT an OHADA member (unlike Benin/CAR/DRC/Congo), but the agent found and verified via ohada.org's own official member list that Comoros IS an OHADA member (ratified 20 Oct 1995) -- a genuine research correction, not a scripted outcome. Delivered: marketentry.facts (Code des Marches Publics 2022 (Loi n22-011/AU) Art.19 creating ARMP, attached to the Presidency; live e-procurement/portal structure at armpcomores.km including a real exclusion-list page; company registration via ANPI/RCCM/Tribunal de Commerce plus OHADA AUSCGIE Art.311 (SARL capital)/Art.387 (SA capital); tax registration via AGID (Administration Generale des Impots et des Domaines, Loi n12-004/AU du 21 juin 2012), independently correcting a stale 'DGI'-only naming assumption to the actual current AGID name) + a governor check per the established universal-check pattern (spec-basis/evidence-completeness) rather than a forced novel flagship, since the agent's own honest assessment found the country's documented mechanisms did not yield a clearly novel independent-shape candidate beyond what the universal checks already cover -- an honest-scope decision consistent with the 'accuracy over novelty' instruction given to all 5 batch agents. Statute.facts: Code du Travail 2012 (Loi n12-12/AU + decret n12-167/PR, amending the 1984 Loi n84-108/PR). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing: rep-spec-basis nil; the certification body named in Code Art.76 not independently located; ANPI's own founding decree/date not independently verified (secondary-source only, ~2008); the 1984 base law and 2012/2019 arretes on business-activity declarations cited only via secondary metadata. Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text (already present in the Benin sibling this pattern was copied from), and separately fixed a genuine pre-existing repo defect unrelated to citations: 7 .cpcache/* build-artifact cache files had been accidentally committed with no .gitignore in place -- added a .gitignore (matching the Bhutan sibling's) and stopped tracking them (confirmed via GitHub compare API as 7 clean file removals, not accidental content loss).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Code des Marches Publics 2022 PDF myself (armpcomores.km, 644KB) and read Art.19 (ARMP creation) and Art.75 7deg (exclusion mechanism) directly -- Art.19's exact 'Il est cree une Autorite de regulation des marches publics...rattachee a la Presidence de l'Union des Comores' text confirmed verbatim, and Art.75 7deg's exact 'sauf prescription de cinq ans' 5-year-exclusion-prescription language confirmed verbatim (note: articles in this PDF are formatted as 'Art.N.-' not 'Article N', requiring a format-aware search after an initial naive grep found nothing); (2) independently re-fetched ohada.org's member-state list myself and confirmed 'Comores' appears on it, corroborating the agent's own research correction rather than just trusting it; (3) independently re-fetched dgi.gouv.km's historique page myself and confirmed 'AGID' / 'Historique de l'AGID' appears, corroborating the naming; (4) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 38 tests / 126 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 38/126/0; (5) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (6) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (7) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the 7 .cpcache/* files show status 'removed' (clean cleanup, not silent data loss) and that the merge touched only the intended scaffold + doc + gitignore files; (8) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-com checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch actor/market-entry-comoros -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-com/merges, commit 317d78d86c526153d2a21a747ea244f32da2f133) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 6cba4ce9673b -> 317d78d86c52 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). Committed and pushed as SEPARATE Bash calls per the iteration-36 workaround.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- third landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/COD/COM done, CAF/COG/CPV still pending land, though CAF and COG's own scaffold agents have already completed and are queued for verification). Axis alternation is now 20 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 38 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 38, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:15:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 39, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-cog", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Republic of the Congo (COG) from a src/culture-only stub, fourth landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV). Delivered: marketentry.facts (Decret n2009-156 du 20 mai 2009 portant Code des Marches Publics, Art.20 creating ARMP attached to the Presidency, Art.17 SS2 grounding DGCMP's a priori control under the finance ministry -- correctly kept as separate authorities like DRC/CAR's own two-body split rather than assumed identical; ARMP's live site (armp.cg, curl blocked by an 'Anubis' anti-bot challenge but WebFetch succeeded) confirming a not-yet-live digitalization status and a currently-empty exclusion list, an honest disclosed finding rather than assumed operational; ACPCE (Loi n16-2017 + Decret n2017-522) for company/RCCM/NIU registration; DGID (impots.cg) for tax, with NIU as the identifier and a live tele-declaration portal distinct from DGID's own under-construction public site) + a governor check built on Art.146's exclusion-sanction mechanism: an exclusion-duration-cap-exceeded check independently verifying a proposed exclusion period against Art.146's exact 5-year statutory maximum, with the court-ordered-definitive-exclusion-on-repeat-violation exception correctly modeled as a distinct escalation path rather than folded into the same cap. Also models niu-registration-unverified as a conditional hold. Statute.facts: OHADA AUSCGIE (independently re-verified: exact title/dates, NOT copied from Benin/CAR/DRC's citations despite the shared supranational source) and Code du Travail (Loi n45/75 du 15 mars 1975, read via curl+tesseract OCR since the primary PDF is a scanned image with no text layer -- French-language OCR successfully applied). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing: specific numeric procurement thresholds (Decret n2009-162/2