found; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (5) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 19 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (6) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cog checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch marketentry-actor-scaffold -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cog/merges, commit d0e115d75b919a3a1f0cfd0c2fd62e11f3fbfe4a) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced b90194d4c02f -> d0e115d75b91 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. Also proactively found and fixed a stale loop-system-dynamics pin (2afaba3a5369 -> 290bc55c66f4, confirmed ahead_by 1 / behind_by 0 via compare API before patching). Committed and pushed as SEPARATE Bash calls per the iteration-36 workaround.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- fourth landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/COD/COM/COG done, CAF/CPV still pending land despite their own scaffold agents having already completed and queued for verification). Axis alternation is now 21 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 39 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 39, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:20:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 40, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-caf", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Central African Republic (CAF) from a src/culture-only stub, fifth landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV). Notable finding: the agent discovered that CAR just enacted a BRAND-NEW Code de la Commande Publique (promulgated 23 Dec 2025, only weeks before this iteration), replacing the old 2008 procurement law's ARMP/DGMP structure with a new three-body split (A.R.C.O.P regulator attached to the Primature / D.G.C.O.P a priori control under Finance / U.G.C.O.P per-contracting-authority unit) -- a genuine, timely research finding, not something that could have been assumed from any prior sibling's pattern. Delivered: marketentry.facts (old Loi n08.017 du 06 juin 2008 confirmed as superseded-but-still-machine-readable reference point, new Code de la Commande Publique as the current law) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: an INCLUSION-ELIGIBILITY workforce-composition test independently recomputing the new Code's 'Marché réservé' (reserved-contract) definition -- eligibility restricted to social-economy legal forms (associations, worker/artisan cooperatives, groupements d'intérêt économique) OR SMEs meeting an OR-combination threshold (>=30% disabled employees, OR >=50% youth, OR >=50% women) -- distinct from every prior sibling (Bulgaria %-formula, Albania flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia boolean membership, Antigua and Barbuda 3-tier value class, Benin bid-margin recompute, Belize struck-off boolean, Barbados expiry-date recompute, Brunei precedence-ordering, Bhutan sector set-membership, Botswana/DRC ordered-tier classification, Congo exclusion-duration-cap) since this is a multi-criterion OR-eligibility test on WORKFORCE COMPOSITION, a genuinely new axis of classification. CAR's OHADA membership independently re-verified (not assumed from Benin/DRC/Congo's precedent) via ohada.org's own member list ('Centrafrique'). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing: CAR's Labour Code (Code du Travail) could not be found/verified -- travail.gouv.cf, droit-afrique.com, FAOLEX, and ILO NATLEX/NORMLEX all returned 403, DDG anti-bot wall hit, WebSearch exhausted -- left out entirely rather than guessed; no national single-window/Guichet-Unique business-formalities agency found (commerce.gouv.cf, pme-artisanat.gouv.cf, plan.gouv.cf, impots.gouv.cf all confirmed non-functional placeholder pages); a representative/director exclusion-extension provision (present in the OLD 2008 Code's Art.17-19) was not confirmed to have a direct equivalent in the NEW Code within the pages read, so not claimed; OHADA Treaty Article 10's exact wording not confirmed (ohada.org's own revised-treaty page skips Article 9 to Article 12 in what was fetched). Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text (disclosed as STILL PRESENT in the Benin sibling itself, out of this iteration's scope to fix retroactively), and fixed a stray inaccurate ':head-role \"ARMP / public procurement\"' key in organization.edn that predated this research (removed to match the reference siblings' shape, since the new Code replaced ARMP with A.R.C.O.P.).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the OLD 2008 Code PDF myself (finances.gouv.cf, ~298KB) -- exact title match 'LOI N 08. 017 PORTANT CODE DE MARCHES PUBLICS ET DELEGATIONS DE SERVICE PUBLIC EN REPUBLIQUE CENTRAFRICAINE'; (2) independently re-fetched ohada.org's member list myself and confirmed 'Centrafrique' appears on it; (3) re-downloaded the NEW Code PDF myself (30MB, genuinely scanned/no-text-layer, confirmed via pdffonts showing zero embedded fonts and pdftotext extracting only 93 bytes) and independently OCR'd it MYSELF using the FRENCH tesseract language pack (tesseract --list-langs confirmed fra IS available in this environment, contradicting the agent's own claim that 'no French pack was available' -- the agent used English-only OCR on French text, a lower-quality path than mine, though it still arrived at correct high-confidence conclusions) -- confirmed page 1's exact title and the SAME genuine OCR ambiguity in the law's serial number ('LOI N 25 0 016', matching the agent's own disclosed MODERATE-confidence uncertainty rather than a discrepancy) via my own independent French-OCR pass; searched pages 9-30 and found and read the EXACT 'Marché réservé' definition on pages 11-12 verbatim, confirming precisely the agent's claimed workforce-composition criteria: 'petites et moyennes entreprises employant au moins 30% de personnes victimes d'handicap ou 50% de jeunes ou 50% de femmes' -- an exact, independently-obtained verbatim match to the flagship check's foundational citation; (4) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 38 tests / 131 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 38/131/0; (5) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (6) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture/data/blueprint.edn/schema/culture.edn untouched via diff --stat; (7) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 20 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (8) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-caf checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch feat/market-entry-statute-actor-caf -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-caf/merges, commit 29887ccb3db0c6a926e473316c6902833da9a3b6) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 9b5d532f0200 -> 29887ccb3db0 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). Committed and pushed as SEPARATE Bash calls per the iteration-36 workaround.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- fifth landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/COD/COM/COG/CAF done, only CPV remains, its own scaffold agent having already completed and queued for verification). Axis alternation is now 22 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 40 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 40, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:30:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 41, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-cpv", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Cabo Verde (CPV) from a src/culture-only stub, sixth and final landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV) dispatched per owner instruction to use subagents for efficient parallel deepening. Delivered: marketentry.facts (ARAP -- Agencia de Regulacao Aquisicoes Publicas, Estatutos established under Decreto-regulamentar structure, replacing an earlier Decreto-lei n15/2008 regime per its own Art.54 revogacao clause; live eCompras/ePCV e-procurement platform at epcv.gov.cv; DNRE for tax/NIF registration (Decreto-Lei n89/2005), honestly disclosed as IN-PERSON-ONLY rather than assumed online after the agent's own research contradicted its initial assumption; DGRNI for company registration (Decreto-Lei n47/2016); Portal Empresa Online confirmed as beta/pilot-only, not fully live) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: a THRESHOLD/BAND-CLASSIFICATION recompute against the Estatuto da ARAP's own Annex fee table (Artigo 43(1)(b)): goods/services and public-works contracts are exempt from ARAP's contract-registration fee up to 2,000,000 CVE, while consulting-services contracts are never exempt (a flat rate applies regardless of value) -- distinct from Botswana/DRC's ORDERED-tier classification (a ranked scale, not a value-band boundary) and from every other prior sibling shape. Deliberately did NOT build the flagship on ARAP's real 'lista de entidades nao elegiveis' (debarment) mechanism despite verifying it exists (Estatuto Artigos 15(k)/17(c)) since no access to its actual current membership was available and fabricating plausible debarred names would violate the no-fabrication rule -- modeled instead as a required-evidence checklist item, mirroring Bhutan's own treatment of its similarly-real-but-partially-unverifiable Debarment Rules. Statute.facts left WITHOUT a Commercial/Companies Code or Labour Code entry -- extensive search (ARAP, DGRNI, Ministry of Family/Labour, OACV, WIPO Lex, ILO NATLEX which 403'd, several .gov.cv hosts with expired/self-signed certs, DDG anti-bot wall) found nothing independently verifiable, an honest empty result rather than a guessed citation. Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md, plus a bare OHADA/French-family 'RCCM' bullet in README.md that does not apply to Cabo Verde's Portuguese-language civil-law system.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded the ARAP_Estatutos.pdf myself (arap.cv, ~722KB) and confirmed via pdffonts it is genuinely a scanned image PDF with zero embedded fonts, matching the agent's claim; independently OCR'd it myself using the PORTUGUESE tesseract language pack (available in this environment) and located Artigo 43.º ('Receitas ... Constituem receitas da ARAP: a) As taxas devidas pela prestacao dos seus servicos; b) Os emolumentos arrecadados atraves dos contratos adjudicados...') and the Annex 'Tabela de emolumentos' on a later page, confirming verbatim the exact exemption clause ('Nos Contratos de locacao, aquisicao de bens moveis e servicos, ate 2.000.000$00 ... Isento') and, on a follow-up OCR pass with different page segmentation, the consulting-services row ('Nos Contratos de servicos de consultoria, igual a 10.000.000$00, 0,5%' -- no exemption language, corroborating the agent's 'never exempt' claim) and independently arriving at the SAME 0,5% rate figure the agent itself flagged as lower-confidence OCR, adding some corroboration via a second independent OCR pass though the underlying image-quality limitation remains; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 39 tests / 135 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 39/135/0; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (4) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (5) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 20 marketentry/statute/doc/deps files and zero culture-catalog files; (6) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cpv checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch agent/cpv-marketentry-actor-scaffold -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cpv/merges, commit 8f3399351543a0cf1cee794189ee6773773b513c) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 572bfaecec29 -> 8f3399351543 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). Committed and pushed as SEPARATE Bash calls per the iteration-36 workaround.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- this closes out the entire 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV all now landed). This batch demonstrates the new parallel-dispatch workflow requested by the owner ('subagent で効率的に深化を進めてください') is viable: 6 countries scaffolded concurrently in roughly the same wall-clock time as 1-2 would have taken sequentially, each independently re-verified with the same rigor as every prior single-agent iteration (primary-source re-fetch, independent OCR where needed, fresh-clone test re-runs, diff-scope verification via GitHub API). Axis alternation is now 23 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 41 iterations -- the prod-ready axis is now meaningfully ahead; a future iteration should consider a real-world-ingest-gap batch next to rebalance, potentially using the same parallel-dispatch pattern for multiple citation additions across different isic catalogs simultaneously.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 41, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:35:00Z"}
