{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 44, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1910", :event/action "Added Poland (:POL) as a 6th jurisdiction to coke.facts/catalog. Notably, the delegated agent discovered upon cloning that a Germany (:DEU) entry had ALREADY been merged into main (commit afb6f545, dated the day before this batch, from an earlier segment of this same overall session predating a context-compaction) -- this was independently confirmed real by the orchestrating session (not a duplicate/hallucinated finding) via GitHub API, and the agent correctly adapted by adding a SIXTH jurisdiction (Poland) rather than colliding with the already-existing fifth. Citations: Rozporzadzenie Ministra Srodowiska z dnia 27 sierpnia 2014 r. (Dz.U. 2014 poz. 1169), Zalacznik ust.1 pkt.3, explicitly naming 'do produkcji koksu' (coke production) as an installation type requiring an environmental permit -- the regulation's own footnote confirms it implements EU Directive 2010/75/EU (IED) Annex I item 1.3, the same EU directive family underlying Germany's own 4. BImSchV citation, giving a genuinely corroborating cross-jurisdiction EU-directive lineage rather than an unrelated citation; and Kodeks pracy (Labour Code, Dz.U. 2023 poz. 1465) Art.207 SS1 (employer responsibility for workplace safety) + Art.226 (mandatory occupational risk assessment/documentation and worker risk-information duty). Honestly omitted raw-material-verification/byproduct-handling entries, matching the KOR/DEU entries' own prior disclosed omission of the same categories.", :event/verification "Both citations independently re-fetched and confirmed verbatim by the orchestrating session directly against dziennikustaw.gov.pl (Poland's official Journal of Laws, plain PDF with embedded text layer, no OCR needed) -- the 2014 regulation's exact Annex line 'do produkcji koksu' confirmed, and the Kodeks pracy's exact Art.207 SS1 text ('Pracodawca ponosi odpowiedzialnosc za stan bezpieczenstwa i higieny pracy w zakladzie pracy') and Art.226 text ('Pracodawca: 1) ocenia i dokumentuje ryzyko zawodowe...') both matched precisely. Also independently confirmed via GitHub API that the pre-existing Germany merge commit (afb6f545dcf5190b6d1ec791e4ca27986dbdfbad, 'Merge: add Germany jurisdiction to coke-oven catalog (4. BImSchV + ArbSchG)') is genuinely real and is the actual current main tip prior to this landing, ruling out agent hallucination or an actual concurrent-session collision. clojure -M:test run in the child repo checkout before (27/75) and after (29/83) landing, both directly and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 29 tests / 83 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via agent-pushed branch add-poland-jurisdiction-catalog -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1910/merges, commit dec89ba07b5e74ebd81b18b79565a17ac8e3f17e) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/coke/facts.cljc + test/coke/facts_test.clj touched) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced afb6f545dcf5 -> dec89ba07b5e (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from the same batched isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (the pre-existing Germany entry was a genuine prior landing, not a false positive to screen out).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "Part of the same 4-catalog parallel batch -- see adjacent entries.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 44, :event/at "2026-07-22T10:50:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 45, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-7820", :event/action "Added South Korea (:kor) as a 6th jurisdiction to staffing.facts/catalog (was USA/Japan/Germany/UK/FRA), fourth and final landing of the 4-catalog parallel batch, closing out the rebalancing toward real-world-ingest-gap after the preceding 6-country prod-ready batch. Citation: the Act on the Protection of Dispatched Workers (파견근로자 보호 등에 관한 법률) Art.6 (파견기간, Dispatch Period) SSSS1-2: a 1-year default dispatch-assignment tenure cap, extendable ONCE by mutual agreement of the dispatching employer/host employer/dispatched worker, with the total period including the extension capped at 2 years -- with SS3's elderly-worker exception (no 2-year cap for workers meeting the Aged Employment Promotion Act's elderly-worker definition) explicitly modeled as NOT universal. The agent tried law.go.kr's English search UI (elaw.klri.re.kr) first and found it genuinely broken (HTTP 500 Java NullPointerException on every POST attempt, with/without session cookies) -- rather than forcing that path or giving up, it used law.go.kr's own machine-readable Open API endpoint (law.go.kr/DRF/lawService.do) to fetch primary-source XML directly, a novel API-discovery workaround for this specific jurisdiction's tooling limitation (analogous to the earlier e-Gov Japan API-behind-JS-SPA pattern, but for a different domain/failure mode).", :event/verification "Citation independently re-fetched and confirmed verbatim by the orchestrating session directly against the same law.go.kr Open API XML endpoint -- Art.6 SS1 exact text ('SS 근로자파견의 기간은 제5조제2항에 해당하는 경우를 제외하고는 1년을 초과하여서는 아니 된다'), SS2 exact text (1-year-per-extension / 2-year-total cap language), and SS3's elderly-worker exception text all matched precisely, confirming the agent's own claimed quotes were not paraphrased or fabricated. clojure -M:dev:test run in a fresh clone with the required kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain} local/root sibling-directory setup (this repo genuinely needs that structure, unlike the other 3 catalogs in this batch): before (41/173) and after (42/190) landing, both directly and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 42 tests / 190 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via agent-pushed branch agent/add-kor-dispatch-tenure-cap (2 commits, the second a genuine self-correction retracting an overclaimed documentation-status comment about the OC=test API parameter) -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7820/merges, commit 025d72af5c3c67f103848d3a6a9404cfd92f1b5b) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/staffing/facts.cljc + test/staffing/facts_test.clj touched) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced c0e5c3b30513 -> 025d72af5c3c (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from the same batched isolated worktree. Also proactively verified and advanced the frequently-drifting loop-system-dynamics pin (290bc55c66f4 -> 30f19b7fda03) alongside all 4 catalog pins, all 5 verified together via a single unfiltered verify-west-pins run.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "This closes out the 4-catalog parallel real-world-ingest-gap batch (apparel/DEU, rolling-stock/DEU, coke/POL, staffing/KOR all landed). Axis alternation is now 23 prod-ready / 22 real-world-ingest-gap across 45 iterations, close to rebalanced. This batch, together with the preceding 6-country prod-ready batch, demonstrates the parallel-subagent-dispatch pattern is now the established default working mode for this loop going forward, per the owner's explicit efficiency instruction -- both axes can sustain 4-6 concurrent agents per batch with the same independent-verification rigor as solo iterations, at roughly the wall-clock cost of 1-2 sequential iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/s